  "id": "automated-speech-recognition",
  "term": "automated speech recognition",
  "definition": "Automated speech recognition is a machine’s ability to turn spoken language carried in an audio signal into words. It is used in areas such as human-computer interaction, assistive technology, and analysis of large collections of speech, and research aims to make it more reliable despite differences in speaker, accent, and background noise.",
